Question 27 — Correct ✅
Domain: Design High-Performing Architectures
Question: A digital media company stores several terabytes of newly generated advertising interaction logs in an Amazon S3 bucket each day. The development team needs to inspect the new dataset quickly by running ad hoc queries before deciding whether the records should enter a downstream transformation workflow. The company wants to minimize infrastructure management and operational effort. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?
Your Answer / Correct Answer: Configure an AWS Glue crawler to catalog the S3 dataset, and use Amazon Athena to run ad hoc SQL queries directly against the data.
Reason: AWS Glue crawlers automatically discover schema metadata in S3, and Amazon Athena is a serverless interactive query service that runs standard SQL directly against S3 objects with zero infrastructure management.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Question 28 — Correct ✅
Domain: Design Secure Architectures
Question: A financial services company has developed its flagship application on AWS Cloud with data security requirements such that the encryption key must be stored in a custom application running on-premises. The company wants to offload the data storage as well as the encryption process to Amazon S3 but continue to use the existing encryption key. Which of the following Amazon S3 encryption options allows the company to leverage Amazon S3 for storing data with given constraints?
Your Answer / Correct Answer: Server-Side Encryption with Customer-Provided Keys (SSE-C)
Reason: With SSE-C, the customer stores and manages the encryption keys (on-premises) and passes the key to S3 with each read/write request, while S3 performs the CPU-intensive encryption and decryption server-side.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Question 29 — Incorrect ❌
Domain: Design High-Performing Architectures
Question: An engineering team wants to examine the feasibility of the user data feature of Amazon EC2 for an upcoming project. Which of the following are true about the Amazon EC2 user data configuration? (Select two)
Your Answer:
By default, user data runs only during the boot cycle when you first launch an instance (Correct)
By default, scripts entered as user data do not have root user privileges for executing (Incorrect)
Correct Answers:
By default, scripts entered as user data are executed with root user privileges.
By default, user data runs only during the boot cycle when you first launch an instance.
Reason: EC2 User Data scripts run only once during the initial launch boot cycle by default, and they always execute as the root user by default (you do not need sudo in user data scripts). Additionally, to modify user data on an existing instance, the instance must first be stopped.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Question 30 — Correct ✅
Domain: Design Secure Architectures
Question: Which of the following IAM policies provides read-only access to the Amazon S3 bucket mybucket and its content?
Your Answer / Correct Answer:
{
   "Version":"2012-10-17",
   "Statement":[
      {
         "Effect":"Allow",
         "Action":["s3:ListBucket"],
         "Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::mybucket"
      },
      {
         "Effect":"Allow",
         "Action":["s3:GetObject"],
         "Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::mybucket/*"
      }
   ]
}
Reason: Bucket-level operations like s3:ListBucket apply to the bucket ARN (arn:aws:s3:::mybucket), whereas object-level operations like s3:GetObject apply to objects inside the bucket (arn:aws:s3:::mybucket/*).
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Question 31 — Correct ✅
Domain: Design High-Performing Architectures
Question: A media company has created an AWS Direct Connect connection for migrating its flagship application to the AWS Cloud. The on-premises application writes hundreds of video files into a mounted NFS file system daily. Post-migration, the company will host the application on an Amazon EC2 instance with a mounted Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. Before the migration cutover, the company must build a process that will replicate the newly created on-premises video files to the Amazon EFS file system. Which of the following represents the MOST operationally efficient way to meet this requirement?
Your Answer / Correct Answer: Configure an AWS DataSync agent on the on-premises server that has access to the NFS file system. Transfer data over the AWS Direct Connect connection to an AWS PrivateLink interface VPC endpoint for Amazon EFS by using a private VIF. Set up an AWS DataSync scheduled task to send the video files to the Amazon EFS file system every 24 hours.
Reason: AWS DataSync natively replicates NFS file systems to Amazon EFS on a recurring schedule, and can route privately over Direct Connect using a Private VIF and an Interface VPC Endpoint (AWS PrivateLink).
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Question 32 — Correct ✅
Domain: Design High-Performing Architectures
Question: A company is developing a global healthcare application that requires the least possible latency for database read/write operations from users in several geographies across the world. The company has hired you as an AWS Certified Solutions Architect Associate to build a solution using Amazon Aurora that offers an effective recovery point objective (RPO) of seconds and a recovery time objective (RTO) of a minute. Which of the following options would you recommend?
Your Answer / Correct Answer: Set up an Amazon Aurora Global Database cluster
Reason: Amazon Aurora Global Database spans multiple AWS Regions with dedicated storage-level replication, delivering an RPO of ~1 second and an RTO of < 1 minute during Regional failover.
